    "Transcribed from the master plan's Ground-Truth Event Log and Part 2b per-clip benchmark table — these are Godrej's own on-screen labels, not model output, so confidence is set uniformly high (0.95) rather than varying per event.",
    "Filenames match the 7 clips in the shared Google Drive folder ('Mumbai Branch - Damage Material RCA'), matched to clip numbers via content + relative file size against the benchmark table's frame counts.",
    "dock_assumed=true on every clip: the master plan states footage spans Docks 06-10 across multiple dates but never maps a specific clip to a specific dock. Docks are assigned here in sequence (06,07,08,09,10,06,07) purely so the dashboard's per-dock aggregation has something real to group by — treat as illustrative, not verified.",
    "product_sku assignments are inferred from each event's plain-language description (e.g. 'cupboard'/'KD panel' -> ABC-123) since the ground-truth table doesn't include SKU data; two events (the dock/vehicle gap and uneven dock level in Clip 1) have no product involved and are left product_sku=null.",
    "Events combining two behaviors on one ground-truth row (e.g. Clip 1's 'Dragging + Improper Handling', Clip 4's 'Rolling and dropping', Clip 6's 'Throwing + stacking') are kept as single multi-label events, matching the master plan's own finding that multi-label incidents are real."
